  "scenario": "A lithium-ion cell plant producing automotive pouch cells has seen capacity retention degrade about 25% faster than spec over the past two months, consistently across production lots. The problem appeared after a facilities change to the dry-room HVAC and an electrolyte-supplier switch. Cell engineers' leading theories are that charging is too aggressive or cells run too hot, so they favor slower charging and more cooling. Early-life coulombic-efficiency readings have looked slightly low. Standard line data read broadly within spec. The charging profile, formation, environmental, and additive systems are all adjustable. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available process controls, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the accelerated fade and what to do about it.",
